<title>GREECE: Bank of Greece drains 200 bln drs of 14-day funds.</title>
<headline>Bank of Greece drains 200 bln drs of 14-day funds.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Greece drained 200 billion drachmas of 14-day funds at 11.90 percent through a fixed interest rate tender on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Payment date is May 7 and maturity value date May 21.</p>
<p>It said submitted bids exceeded the amount tendered and the central bank satisfied all bids at 5.15 percent.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
